    "final_answer": "I have all the information I need to provide a complete answer.\n\n**Key Information from WolframAlpha:**\n\nThe image in the comparison table clearly shows:\n- **3 months and 6 days (3 个月 6 天)** is required with **1500 kcal/day** intake (81% of BMR)\n- This is at a sedentary activity level\n- The target weight loss is 17 kg\n\nAdditional supporting data:\n- For 175 cm, 40 year old male at 90 kg, sedentary:\n  - Maintenance calories: ~2783 kcal/day\n  - BMR: ~1852 kcal/day (since 1500 = 81% of BMR)\n- Daily caloric deficit: ~1283 kcal/day\n- Ideal weight: 70 kg (so losing 17 kg gets him close to ideal weight)\n\n## Final Answer\n\nAccording to WolframAlpha's calculation, for a **40-year-old male, 175 cm tall, currently weighing 90 kg**, consuming **1500 calories per day** while maintaining a sedentary activity level, it would take approximately **3 months and 6 days** (about 98 days) to lose **17 kg**.\n\n**Important caveats:**\n- This time frame assumes the person remains sedentary throughout the weight loss\n- The BMR was calculated using Mifflin-St Jeor equation for males: 10×weight + 6.25×height − 5×age + 5\n- 1500 kcal/day represents 81% of his basal metabolic rate, which is considered a moderate (but sustainable) caloric restriction\n- A safer/slower approach would be 6 months at 2033 kcal/day (110% of BMR), which is within the recommended healthy weight loss range\n- A more aggressive approach of 2 months 17 days at 1206 kcal/day (65% of BMR) is also shown, though 2 weeks at any reasonable calorie level would be unattainable",
